Q: C++ efficient method of formatting std::cout A: <blockquote>
<p>How would one more cleanly format this while keeping spaces?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I wouldn't print out any hard-coded space characters at all. I would let <code>std::cout</code> pad out the values as needed, via the <a href="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/manip/setw.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>std::setw</code></a> and <a href="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/manip/setfill.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>std::setfill</code></a> stream manipulators, eg:</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;
#include &lt;iomanip&gt;

int main() {
    std::cout &lt;&lt; &quot;Calculator App&quot; &lt;&lt; std::endl;

    double num1, num2;
    std::cin &gt;&gt; num1;
    std::cin &gt;&gt; num2;

    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::setfill(' ');
    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::left &lt;&lt; std::setw(15)
              &lt;&lt; &quot;First number:&quot;
              &lt;&lt; num1
              &lt;&lt; std::endl;
    std::cout &lt;&lt; std::left &lt;&lt; std::setw(15)
              &lt;&lt; &quot;Second number:&quot;
              &lt;&lt; num2;
              &lt;&lt; std::endl;
    return 0;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Output:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>Calculator App
First number:  5.3
Second number: 81.1
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://onlinegdb.com/lP9biFLUd" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Online Demo</a></p>
<p>Since <code>&quot;First number:&quot;</code> and <code>&quot;Second number:&quot;</code> are less than 15 characters in length, the fill character <code>' '</code> will be output automaatically, eg:</p>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| F | i | r | s | t |   | n | u | m | b | e | r | : |   |   | 5 | . | 3 | ⏎ |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                                      ^   ^
                                                    fill chars

+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| S | e | c | o | n | d |   | n | u | m | b | e | r | : |   | 8 | 1 | . | 1 | ⏎ |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                                          ^
                                                      fill char
</code></pre>
